Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||12-09-2001||08:52 PM||||I've seen modded cases to include extra fans etc.. but this whole windows with neon lights inside is a bit much for me.<P>I built a liquid cooled computer 2 years ago, and it required a few case modifications.. but nothing like that.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||12-09-2001||09:05 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.virtual-hideout.net/articles/hx08/index3.shtml" TARGET=_blank>http://www.virtual-hideout.net/articles/hx08/index3.shtml</A> <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B>Using the plastic bowl to improve air flow and reduce turbulence wasn't my idea. I saw some guys on the Web doing this, so I thought why not give it a try. Turn my kitchen upside down looking for that perfect plastic bowl. (Sorry mom!!!) Finally found these bowls! Locals should recognise them easily as they are used to store the cold dessert we call "ICED KACANG"!!! They are fairly soft and easy to work with. A scissors or penknife should be able to cut them to the required diameter and depth. Put some masking tape on the clear plastic to give it that same colour as the bezel. Looks COOL!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>NUFF SAID.<P>------------------<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>     <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 12-09-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000004||8Ball||12-09-2001||11:52 PM||||Cases like those make me a pretty descent living  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> When I am not "The Virii Guy" and "Uber Tech" as my co workers love to call me. I am modding cases for our most valued (richest) customers  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>E.B.||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||12-10-2001||01:45 PM||||I spent some time reading that site more, and a lot of the painted cases look really sweet.. I just thought the masking tape part was funny.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>but still, neons inside a computer....?<BR>Oh well, I can think of worse things they could do..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I wonder how you'd rice up a computer though.. can't use a bigger heatsink and fan, that'd actually be functional.. maybe some fake fan holes? or chrome striping around the case & fans??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I'll post a pic when I get home (haven't got the link here) but it's a computer with a custom paint job, looks like black chrome. it's amazing....<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||12-10-2001||02:04 PM||||ok, I was bored. I found the link.. check this out!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.pc-workshop.net/articles/paint101/thumb/paint101-t.jpg"> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.pc-workshop.net/articles/paint101/paint101-t.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.pc-workshop.net/articles/paint101/paint101-t.jpg</A> <P>I'm almost tempted to buy a new case and paint it, so it looks that good.. my current case is plain grey, with a dark grey panel on the front.. looks nice, but it's boring.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
